{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebDeltaRule","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebDeltaRule","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebThresholdBridge"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebDeltaRule.e_mul_elt_eq_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebDeltaRule.e_mul_elt_eq_smul","kind":"theorem","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebDeltaRule.lean#L164-L170","doc":"**The measured δ rule, proved at the normal-form index.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebDeltaRule.word_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebDeltaRule.word_split","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebDeltaRule.lean#L128-L160","doc":"**The instantiation.** If `k ∈ I` and no element of `I` is `k-1`, the word\nof `(I,J)` splits as `pre ++ k :: post` with every letter of `pre` far from\n`k` — exactly the hypothesis of `e_mul_prod_eq_smul`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebDeltaRule.mem_take_lt_getElem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebDeltaRule.mem_take_lt_getElem","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebDeltaRule.lean#L117-L124","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebDeltaRule.mem_zipWith_exists","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebDeltaRule.mem_zipWith_exists","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebDeltaRule.lean#L103-L115","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebDeltaRule.flatten_zipWith_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebDeltaRule.flatten_zipWith_split","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebDeltaRule.lean#L92-L100","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebDeltaRule.zipWith_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebDeltaRule.zipWith_split","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebDeltaRule.lean#L86-L90","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebDeltaRule.le_sub_two_of_lt_of_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebDeltaRule.le_sub_two_of_lt_of_ne","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebDeltaRule.lean#L79-L83","doc":"If `i < k` and `i ≠ k-1` then `i ≤ k-2`. The arithmetic step behind\n\"`k-1 ∉ I` makes every earlier block far from `k`\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebDeltaRule.far_of_le_sub_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebDeltaRule.far_of_le_sub_two","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebDeltaRule.lean#L67-L77","doc":"Being two or more below `k` is exactly \"far from `k`\" in the sense\n`e_farCommute` wants. ","signatureChunk":0}]}